        - HIGH (applied): Explain why the model uses a non-centered parameterization
            - One short paragraph in Loop D before the model shorthand: when tau is small, the centered form effect[s] ~ Normal(mu, tau) creates a narrow neck (the "funnel") that NUTS struggles with because the geometry changes scale with tau. The non-centered form effect[s] = mu + tau * z[s] with z[s] ~ Normal(0, 1) keeps the latent space at unit scale and lets tau vary freely. This avoids divergences, especially when between-segment heterogeneity is small.
            - Reference: Betancourt and Girolami on hierarchical models (cite by topic, not by URL, to keep the chapter self-contained).
            - Added as a "Why non-centered" paragraph just before the model shorthand in Loop D Try, including the funnel geometry argument and the citation by topic.
