                - per-segment shrinkage = (independent point estimate - posterior mean) / (independent point estimate - mu_posterior_mean), computed on the logit scale or the probability scale, for each segment
                - an explicit "with n thousands per segment, shrinkage is X percent; with n hundred per segment shrinkage would be much larger" is fine, but only if backed by a quick rerun at smaller n in the notebook.
            - Optional small extension: add a second hierarchical fit at n_per_segment around 100 to make the regularization visible. Keep the first fit as the baseline so the contrast is concrete.
